    "body": "Thanks for finding these issues!\n\n> The select button slot is not expected to take its fallback. It should take the first button element child, if any exists, and that's it.\n\nDoes this mean I should remove everything after the \"otherwise\" in this sentence?\n\nIt is [expected](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#expected) to take the first child element of the [select](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-select-element) if the first child element is a [button](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-button-element), otherwise the [select fallback button text](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#select-fallback-button-text).\n\nI opened a PR: https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12158\n",
